  <ferc:AddressWhereCorporateBooksAreKept id="f-1" contextRef="c-1">645 Hamilton Street, Allentown, PA 18101</ferc:AddressWhereCorporateBooksAreKept>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock id="f-2" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1.None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock id="f-3" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2.None.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock id="f-4" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;3.None.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock id="f-5" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;4.None.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock id="f-6" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;5.None.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="f-7" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;6. The Respondent was authorized by the FERC at Docket No. ES26-3-000 to issue, from time to time, from January 1, 2026 through December 31, 2027, up to $1.0 billion of promissory notes and other evidence of secured and unsecured short-term indebtedness. &lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;At June 30, 2026, the Respondent had a $750 million credit facility syndicated with a group of banks that expires in December 2030. This facility was initially authorized by the PUC at Securities Certificates No. S-2010-2183912. The PUC authorized the most recent extension of the facility at Securities Certificate No. S-2019-3009986. Under this facility, the Respondent has the ability to make cash borrowings and to request the lenders to issue letters of credit. At June 30, 2026, the Respondent had no cash borrowings and $6 million of letters of credit outstanding under this facility. &lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;At June 30, 2026, the Respondent maintained a commercial paper program for up to $750 million. Commercial paper issuances are supported by the Respondent&#8217;s syndicated credit facility based on available capacity. The Respondent had no commercial paper outstanding at June 30, 2026. &lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On May 12, 2026, the Respondent issued $500 million of 5.75% First Mortgage Bonds due 2056 that settled on May 15, 2026. This issuance was authorized at Securities Certificate No. S-2024-3048615.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;See Note 7 of the Notes to Financial Statements for further discussion of financing activities.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="f-8" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;7. None.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="f-9" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;8.During the first quarter of 2026, non-union personnel received a 3% wage increase.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="f-10" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;9.Reference is made to Note 10 of the Notes to Financial Statements for information concerning the Respondent's commitments and contingent liabilities and environmental matters.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock id="f-11" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;10.None.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantChangesRelatedToRespondentCompanyAppearingInAnnualReportToStockholdersTextBlock id="f-12" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;12.Not applicable.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantChangesRelatedToRespondentCompanyAppearingInAnnualReportToStockholdersTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock id="f-13" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;13. None.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock id="f-14" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;14.Not applicable.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfApplicableNotesTextBlock id="f-15" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;As permitted by the FERC for the 2026 FERC Form No. 3-Q, the Notes to Financial Statements set forth below are principally from the Respondent's SEC Form 10-Q which was filed with the SEC on August 7, 2026 and does not reflect updated information, except for Note 1 and 18. Note 1 was modified to update the basis of presentation for FERC reporting. Note 18 was modified to update supplemental disclosures for Cash Flows. Where appropriate, the Notes to Financial Statements discuss PPL Electric on a stand alone basis. References to "PPL" or "PPL and its subsidiaries" are retained in those instances where it is appropriate to discuss at the parent/total company level or where referencing PPL Electric on a stand alone basis would not result in a complete disclosure. Management has evaluated the impact of events occurring after June 30, 2026 up to August 7, 2026, the date that PPL Electric&#8217;s U.S. GAAP financial statements were issued and has updated such evaluation through August 25, 2026. These financial statements include all necessary adjustments and disclosures resulting from these evaluations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;1. Interim Financial Statements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;(All Registrants)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Capitalized terms and abbreviations appearing in the unaudited combined notes to condensed financial statements are defined in the glossary. Dollars are in millions, except per share data, unless otherwise noted. The specific Registrant to which disclosures are applicable is identified in parenthetical headings in italics above the applicable disclosure or within the applicable disclosure for each Registrant's related activities and disclosures. Within combined disclosures, amounts are disclosed for any Registrant when significant.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;The accompanying unaudited condensed financial statements have been prepared in accordance with GAAP for interim financial information and with the instructions to Form 10-Q and Article&#160;10 of Regulation S-X and, therefore, do not include all of the information and footnote disclosures required by GAAP for complete financial statements. In the opinion of management, all adjustments considered necessary for a fair presentation in accordance with GAAP are reflected in the condensed financial statements. All adjustments are of a normal recurring nature, except as otherwise disclosed. Each Registrant's Balance Sheet at December&#160;31, 2025 is derived from that Registrant's 2025 audited Balance Sheet. The financial statements and notes thereto should be read in conjunction with the financial statements and notes contained in each Registrant's 2025 Form 10-K. The results of operations for the three and six months ended June&#160;30, 2026 are not necessarily indicative of the results to be expected for the full year ending December&#160;31, 2026 or other future periods, because results for interim periods can be disproportionately influenced by various factors, developments and seasonal variations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:161%"&gt;The financial statements are prepared in accordance with the Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States, prescribed by the FERC and adopted by the PUC. Other general purpose financial statements issued by the Respondent are prepared in accordance with GAAP.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:151%"&gt;Significant differences in classifications of items on the Respondent's Form 10-Q are as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:32.233%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:32.233%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:32.234%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:1.5pt;margin-top:1.65pt;padding-left:0.02pt;padding-right:0.02pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:151%"&gt;Reporting Classifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:1.5pt;margin-top:1.65pt;padding-left:0.02pt;padding-right:0.02pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:151%"&gt;FERC Reporting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:1.5pt;margin-top:1.65pt;padding-left:0.02pt;padding-right:0.02pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:151%"&gt;GAAP Reporting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Investments in subsidiaries and associated equity earnings of subsidiary companies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Reported in Investment in Subsidiary Companies (123.1) and Equity in Earnings of Subsidiary Companies (418.1)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Reported in Retained Earnings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Unappropriated undistributed subsidiary earnings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Reported in Unappropriated Undistributed Subsidiary Earnings (216.1)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Reported in Retained Earnings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Balance Sheet presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Reported in order of Uniform System of Accounts (18 CFR Part 101) account number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Reported in order of liquidity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Prepayments of federal income taxes (including effectively settled tax positions)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Reported in Accounts Receivable from Associated Companies (146)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Reported in Accounts Receivable - Other&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Deferred tax assets and liabilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-