    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The information below includes the rate order or document number and the period of amortization, if applicable, for each regulatory asset listed on page 232.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Pension and postretirement medical plants:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">PPL's pension and postretirement medical plans, in which PPL Electric participates, are remeasured each year as of December 31 to reflect the funded status of those plans. These actuarial amounts would normally be charged to Other Comprehensive Income under ASC 715, but are charged to, and amortized from, a regulatory asset for a rate regulated business. Due to the pension and postretirement process, the credits are to various 107, 128, 228 and 926 accounts. See Note 9 of the Notes to Financial Statements for additional information.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization Period: Not Applicable.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Smart Meter Rider:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Represents the net under collection, plus related interest, of the Company's retail Smart Meter Rider (SMR), as set forth in the PA PUC's Final Order entered June 24, 2010, at Docket No. M-2009-2123945. This amount is classified in Account 182.3 when the balance in the account is a net asset, or in Account 254 when the balance in the account is a net liability. Also represented are the deferred costs related to the Smart Meter Plan. On June 30, 2014, PPL Electric filed its final Smart Meter Plan with the PA PUC. In that plan, PPL Electric proposed to replace all of its current meters with advanced meters that meet the Act 129 requirements. It proposed to recover these costs through the SMR which the PA PUC previously approved for recovery of such costs. Full deployment of the new meters was substantially completed at the end of 2019. Effective July 1, 2026, Smart Meter recovery will be included in the new base rates per the PUC Order on Docket R-2025-3057164.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization Period: Not Applicable.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Distribution System Improvement Charge:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents the net under collection of the Company's retail Distribution System Improvement Charge (DSIC), as set forth by Docket No. P-2012-2325034. This amount is classified in Account 182.3 when the balance in the account is a net asset, or in Account 254 when the balance in the account is a net liability.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization Period: Not Applicable.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Storm Damage Expense Rider:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Represents the net under collection, plus related interest, of the Company's retail Storm Damage Expense Rider (SDER). PPL Electric filed Supplement No. 130 in response to the PA PUC's final rate case order in December 2012 at Docket No. R-2012-2290597. The SDER reflects the costs of PA PUC reportable storms greater or less than the amount included in base rates. On April 3, 2014, the PA PUC issued a final order approving the SDER. Per the PUC Order on Docket R-2025-3057164, the amount of storm damage expense included in base rates is set to $32 million. The over or under collection is classified in Account 182.3 when the balance in the account is a net asset, or in Account 254 when the balance in the account is a net liability.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization Period: Not Applicable.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Taxes recoverable through future rates (non-plant):</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents the difference in the provision for deferred income taxes on non-plant liabilities and the amount that is recorded under Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP). This difference represents a tax benefit flowed through to the customer that will be recovered through future rates.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization Period: Not Applicable.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents incremental expenses deferred for those costs incurred in order to prepare, apply, administer, and otherwise execute on Company's Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act (IIJA) funding opportunities, as set forth by the PA PUC's Docket No. P-2022-3032929.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization Period: Three years beginning July 1st, 2026</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Act 129 Phase V:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-bottom:7pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents amounts deferred related to the development of Phase V of the Energy Efficiency &amp; Conservation Plan for ACT 129. The PA PUC has historically allowed deferral of costs relating to plan and program development. See approval on Docket No. M-2014-2424864. These deferred costs will be recovered over 5 years beginning in June 2026.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">TCJA Temporary Negative Surcharge:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">As a result of the reduced U.S. federal corporate income tax rate as enacted by the TCJA, the PAPUC ruled that these tax benefits should be refunded to customers. The impacts of the lower U.S. federal corporate income tax rate are included in base rates effective July 1, 2026. Prior to new base rates going into effect on July 1, 2026, PPL Electric over-refunded customers for the impact of the lower U.S. federal corporate income tax rates. PPL Electric intends to address this remaining balance for recovery in a future proceeding.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">February 13, 2024 Extraordinary Storm:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents amounts deferred related to the extraordinary storm on February 13, 2024. These costs will be recovered through the SDER rate over three years starting in January 2025.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Storm Damage Excess Deferral:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Represents amounts that will cause the expenses to be recovered in the 2025 SDER to be in excess of the 3% cap on projected distribution revenue per docket R-2012-2290597. These amounts shall be deferred and are subject to recovery in a subsequent base rate case under Section 1308. Amortization Period: $11 million to amortize over three year period beginning July 1st, 2026 as a result of the PUC order on Docket R-2025-3057164. The remaining balance is subject to recovery in future rate case.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">IT Reinvention Initiative:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Represents incremental IT costs associated with PPL IT's Reinvention initiative. These incremental costs are recorded as a non current regulatory asset to be deferred and recovered within future rates. Per the Order on Docket R-2025-3057164, recovery of these costs was approved.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Amortization Period: Amortization to occur over useful life of asset.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">November 21, 2024 Extraordinary Storm:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents amounts deferred related to the extraordinary storm on November 21, 2024. These costs will be recovered through the SDER rate over three years starting in January 2026.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Rate Case Deferred Costs:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Represents amounts deferred related to the 2025 rate case. Per the Order on Docket R-2025-3057164, recovery of these costs was approved over three years starting in July 2026.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Universal Service Rider:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents the net over collection, plus related interest, of the Company's retail Universal Service Rider, as set forth in the PA PUC's Opinion and Order entered December 6, 2007, at Docket No. R-00072155. This amount is classified in Account 182.3 when the balance in the account is a net asset, or in Account 254 when the balance in the account is a net liability.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization Period: Not Applicable</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The information below includes the rate order or document number and the period of amortization, if applicable, for each regulatory liability listed on page 278.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Accumulated Deferred Investment Tax Credits:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Represents deferred taxes on the book deferral of investment tax credits. Investment tax credits (&#8220;ITC&#8221;) amortize over the average useful book life of the electric utility property to which the credits relate. As customers receive the tax benefit of ITC amortization, the deferred taxes reverse.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Taxes refundable through future rates:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents the difference in the provision of deferred income taxes for regulated plant assets and the amount that is recorded under GAAP. The difference represents tax expense previously funded by the customer that will be returned to the customer through rates over the book life of the plant assets to which it relates.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization Period: Ongoing&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Generation Supply Charge:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents the net over collection, plus related interest, of the Company's retail Generation Supply Charge (GSC), as set forth in the PA PUC's Final Order on the Generation Supply Charge entered May 17, 2007, at Docket No. P-00062227. This amount is classified in Account 182.3 when the balance in the account is a net asset, or in Account 254 when the balance in the account is a net liability.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization Period: June 1, 2025 through May 31, 2029</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Act 129 Energy Efficiency &amp; Conservation:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Represents the net over collection of the Company&#8217;s retail Phase V Energy Efficiency &amp; Conservation Plan for the Act 129 program, as approved by the PA PUC on May 26, 2026 at Docket No. M-2025-3057329, effective June 1, 2026 through May 31, 2031. The deferral of the initial Phase V costs is being amortized over the Plan&#8217;s five-year period. This amount is classified in Account 182.3 when the balance in the account is a net asset, or in Account 254 when the balance in the account is a net liability.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Amortization Period: June 1, 2026 through May 31, 2031</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Competitive Enhancement Rider:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Represents the net over collection, plus related interest, of the Company's Competitive Enhancement Rider (CER), to recover costs of customer education programs. The CER was approved in the 2012 PPL Electric Utilities Rate Case per the PA PUC's Final Order entered Dec 28, 2012, at Docket No. R-2012-2290597. Effective July 1, 2026, CER recovery will be included in the new base rates per the PUC Order on Docket R-2025-3057164. This amount is classified in Account 182.3 when the balance in the account is a net asset, or in Account 254 when the balance in the account is a net liability.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization Period: Not Applicable</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Transmission Formula Rate:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents the net over collection, plus related interest, of the Company's Transmission Formula Rate, as set forth by FERC Docket No. ER08-1457-000. This amount is classified in Account 182.3 when the balance in the account is a net asset, or in Account 254 when the balance in the account is a net liability.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization Period: Not Applicable</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Taxes refundable through future rates (non-plant):</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents the difference in the provision of deferred income taxes for regulated non-plant assets and the amount that is recorded under GAAP. The difference represents tax expense previously funded by the customer that will be returned to the customer over the amortization period approved by the commission for non-plant assets, which is typically one year.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization Period: 1 year</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:9pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Taxes refundable through future rates (estimated tax rate changes):</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents the same type of activity described in the footnote to Line 2, Column (a). This activity is separately stated because it represents the estimated impact of future phased-in income tax rate changes for years 2024-2031, which are not yet effective for tax return purposes, and therefore not yet included in customer rates to be refunded. As a new income tax rate becomes effective each year, the results of the income tax rate change will be included with the regulatory liability activity on Line 2.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization Period: Not Applicable</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Transmission Service Charge:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents the net over collection, plus related interest, of the Company's retail Transmission Service Charge (TSC), as set forth in the PA PUC's Final Order on the Remand Filing entered July 25, 2007, at Docket No. R-00049255. This amount is classified in Account 182.3 when the balance in the account is a net asset, or in Account 254 when the balance in the account is a net liability.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization Period: Not Applicable</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Distribution System Improvement Charge:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents the net over collection of the Company's retail Distribution System Improvement Charge (DSIC), as set forth by Docket No. P-2012-2325034. This amount is classified in Account 182.3 when the balance in the account is a net asset, or in Account 254 when the balance in the account is a net liability. Amortization Period: Not Applicable</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">In general, sales to customers engaged in wholesale or retail trade, the professions, finance, real estate, insurance or providing services to the public are classified as commercial.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">In general, sales to customers engaged in manufacturing, mining or processing are classified as industrial.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
